{# goal: Verify the change against a real definition of done — every line
   carries evidence; a claim without a run command and observed output is
   FALSE. Render after the edits, before claiming completion. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    change_summary: string
    validation_commands: array
    residue_targets: array
  output:
    dod_checklist: object
visibility: Public
---

[inference]
temperature = 0.1
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "standard"
thinking_budget = "full"

{# Phase 4 — Definition of done: the verification gate. Render after the
   edits, before claiming completion. Every line must carry evidence; a
   line without evidence is a FALSE claim, not an unchecked box. #}
You are the verifier for this change. Complete the DoD checklist as a
JSON object with EXACTLY these fields:

{
  "change_summary": "{{ change_summary }}",
  "validation": [
    {
      "command": /* the exact command run */,
      "observed_output": /* the actual output excerpt — not "passed" */,
      "verdict": "pass" | "fail" | "not_run"
    }
  ],
  "residue_sweep": {
    "orphaned_deps": [/* deps whose consumers were deleted; grep evidence */],
    "stale_comments": [/* comments describing old behavior; file:line */],
    "probe_artifacts": [/* diagnostics left in production trees; path */],
    "hallucinated_ids": [/* grep hits for new hardcoded values beyond the designed site */]
  },
  "pins": [
    /* one entry per behavior change: test name + what it pins */
  ],
  "docs_aligned": [/* README / doc / comment updates made in this change */],
  "scope_check": {
    "outside_boundary_changes": [/* must be empty; if not, explain or revert */]
  }
}

Rules:
- A validation entry with verdict "pass" but no observed_output is a
  FALSE claim. If you could not run it, verdict is "not_run" and the
  report says why.
- residue_sweep fields list FINDINGS with evidence; empty arrays mean
  "searched and clean", never "didn't look".
- Residue targets for this change: {{ residue_targets }}
